-What did she want?
-[chuckles]

263
00:16:37,464 --> 00:16:39,667
He's got a new fighter
he wants to showcase.

264
00:16:39,701 --> 00:16:41,201
-Yeah, The Bomber.

265
00:16:41,235 --> 00:16:43,070
He's big,
he hits like a motherfucker.

266
00:16:43,103 --> 00:16:44,639
He's a good wrestler.

267
00:16:44,672 --> 00:16:47,509
I heard some guys
talking about him at the gym.

268
00:16:50,110 --> 00:16:53,648
Look, the other night,
I was out of line.

269
00:16:53,681 --> 00:16:54,949
I just needed to cool down.

270
00:16:54,983 --> 00:16:56,149
-Don't worry about it.

271
00:16:56,183 --> 00:16:58,786
It's all good, okay?

272
00:16:58,820 --> 00:17:00,522
Come on, let's go upstairs.

273
00:17:00,555 --> 00:17:02,690
Talk about these fights.

274
00:17:04,659 --> 00:17:05,693
So the other night,

275
00:17:05,727 --> 00:17:08,061
we just bought ourselves
some time with Emerson.

276
00:17:08,095 --> 00:17:10,364
But the first chance he gets,

277
00:17:10,397 --> 00:17:12,934
you know he's gonna
come down on all of us.

278
00:17:12,967 --> 00:17:14,201
[cork pops]

279
00:17:15,003 --> 00:17:16,036
-So we hit him first?

280
00:17:16,069 --> 00:17:17,906
-Oh, yeah.
[liquor pouring]

281
00:17:17,939 --> 00:17:21,208
But we do it smart.
Keep him happy,

282
00:17:21,241 --> 00:17:23,377
make the payments on time.

283
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:26,915
In the meantime,
we make our moves.

284
00:17:26,948 --> 00:17:28,550
-What about the fights?

285
00:17:28,583 --> 00:17:30,518
-[sips]

286
00:17:30,552 --> 00:17:32,620
Put them on next week
as scheduled.

287
00:17:32,654 --> 00:17:35,823
We need the cash flow coming in
to keep Emerson off our back.

288
00:17:35,857 --> 00:17:38,292
Fifty grand a month, remember?

289
00:17:38,325 --> 00:17:41,328
You still got your contacts
at the PD?

290
00:17:41,361 --> 00:17:43,063
-I do.

291
00:17:43,096 --> 00:17:44,999
-Want you to find
an old friend of mine.

292
00:17:45,033 --> 00:17:47,100
Mr. Kwan.

293
00:17:47,134 --> 00:17:48,803
He's an information broker.

294
00:17:48,836 --> 00:17:50,137
[paper rips]

295
00:17:50,170 --> 00:17:51,839
He used to move
with some big cats in Chinatown

296
00:17:51,873 --> 00:17:53,140
back in the day.

297
00:17:53,173 --> 00:17:54,542
Did some time
for armed robbery.

298
00:17:54,576 --> 00:17:55,810
Should be able
to track him down.

299
00:17:55,843 --> 00:17:57,444
-You got it.

300
00:17:57,477 --> 00:17:59,747
-Who are you fighting Friday?

301
00:18:02,784 --> 00:18:06,253
-Tank. He's a tough cunt.

302
00:18:07,922 --> 00:18:09,924
-They're all tough cunts, Tommy.

303
00:18:09,958 --> 00:18:12,760
The question is,
can you take him?

304
00:18:12,794 --> 00:18:15,863
-I'll knock out
anybody you put in front of me.

305
00:18:17,065 --> 00:18:19,499
-He's just like his old man.

306
00:18:19,534 --> 00:18:23,605
All right. I'll look over
the rest of the roster.

307
00:18:23,638 --> 00:18:26,373
Make sure we got
some exciting fights to put on.

308
00:18:26,406 --> 00:18:28,743
-So you gonna stick around?

309
00:18:32,212 --> 00:18:35,482
-His father saved my life.

310
00:18:35,516 --> 00:18:38,086
And Clay Emerson
almost ended it.

311
00:18:38,118 --> 00:18:41,556
So yeah,
I'm sticking around.

312
00:18:41,589 --> 00:18:43,524
[mysterious music]

313
00:18:46,159 --> 00:18:49,897
[helicopter blades chopping]

314
00:18:51,298 --> 00:18:53,266
[cheers and whoops]

315
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,003
-Hey. How you doing?
-How you doing?

316
00:18:55,036 --> 00:18:57,204
Good to see you.

317
00:18:57,237 --> 00:18:58,873
How are you doing?

318
00:18:58,906 --> 00:19:01,141
Enjoy the fight, all right?

319
00:19:02,610 --> 00:19:03,911
How's it going?

320
00:19:05,013 --> 00:19:07,115
How you been?
All right?

321
00:19:07,147 --> 00:19:08,148
It's going to be
a good night of fights.

322
00:19:08,181 --> 00:19:10,551
[punch thrown]

323
00:19:11,786 --> 00:19:12,787
-[shouting indistinctly]

324
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:14,287
-Motherfucker!

325
00:19:14,321 --> 00:19:17,091
-[Bender] Emerson's not here,
just that wack job Doyle.

326
00:19:17,125 --> 00:19:18,726
-Come on.

327
00:19:20,895 --> 00:19:22,229
-[grunts]
[strikes blows]

328
00:19:22,262 --> 00:19:24,565
[knee strikes]
[head slams]

329
00:19:25,800 --> 00:19:27,602
-Tommy's up next.

330
00:19:27,635 --> 00:19:30,872
Tell him to stay cool
when he sees Doyle.

331
00:19:34,241 --> 00:19:35,743
-[Boxer grunts] Yeah!

332
00:19:39,246 --> 00:19:41,248
[body thuds]

333
00:19:41,849 --> 00:19:42,884
[punches thrown]

334
00:19:42,917 --> 00:19:44,085
-[shouts] Yeah!

335
00:19:44,118 --> 00:19:45,485
All right.

336
00:19:45,520 --> 00:19:46,954
[claps]

337
00:19:46,988 --> 00:19:50,692
[audience clamoring]

338
00:19:50,725 --> 00:19:53,695
[muffled intense music]

339
00:19:53,728 --> 00:19:54,796
[muffled thumping]

340
00:19:54,829 --> 00:19:56,931
-[Doyle] Come on, Bomber.

341
00:20:06,841 --> 00:20:09,510
-[Virgil] [softly]
All right. Here we go.

342
00:20:16,249 --> 00:20:17,852
[slaps]
Get your ass in the game.

343
00:20:17,885 --> 00:20:19,954
[punches on locker]

344
00:20:22,289 --> 00:20:24,391
-Lewis, Lewis.

345
00:20:24,424 --> 00:20:25,727
Is he okay?
-[Virgil] Oh, yeah.

346
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:28,096
-You're up, Tommy.

347
00:20:28,129 --> 00:20:29,997
-[Tommy] How's the crowd?

348
00:20:30,031 --> 00:20:31,866
-Ready for the main event.

349
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:35,503
-Emerson there?

350
00:20:35,536 --> 00:20:36,904
-No.

351
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:40,742
But his man Doyle is.

352
00:20:41,976 --> 00:20:46,013
Atlas said keep cool.
All right?

353
00:20:46,047 --> 00:20:48,482
Concentrate on the fight.

354
00:20:49,784 --> 00:20:51,886
[upbeat hype music]

355
00:20:51,919 --> 00:20:53,353
-[man] Let's go, yeah!

356
00:20:53,386 --> 00:20:55,823
[audience cheering continues]

357
00:21:03,363 --> 00:21:05,767
[audience whistling]

358
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,869
[man] You can do it,
motherfucker!

359
00:21:07,902 --> 00:21:10,204
-Ladies and gentlemen!

360
00:21:10,238 --> 00:21:13,508
Get your drinks,
place your bets,

361
00:21:13,541 --> 00:21:18,311
and let's get ready
for the fight of the night!

362
00:21:18,345 --> 00:21:19,279
[audience cheering]

363
00:21:19,312 --> 00:21:20,815
-Let's go!

364
00:21:20,848 --> 00:21:23,283
In the blue corner,

365
00:21:23,316 --> 00:21:25,987
the Asian sensation,

366
00:21:26,020 --> 00:21:28,089
Big Tank!

367
00:21:28,122 --> 00:21:29,356
[audience cheering]

368
00:21:29,389 --> 00:21:30,925
-I'm gonna bury you
tonight, Tommy.

369
00:21:30,958 --> 00:21:32,760
You're a fucking dead man!

370
00:21:32,794 --> 00:21:37,064
-And in the red corner,
the one, the only,

371
00:21:37,098 --> 00:21:40,201
Tommy Masterson!

372
00:21:40,234 --> 00:21:42,335
[upbeat hype music continues]

373
00:21:42,369 --> 00:21:44,806
All right.
You know the drill.

374
00:21:44,839 --> 00:21:47,909
No refs.
No judges.

375
00:21:47,942 --> 00:21:49,342
We don't keep score.

376
00:21:49,376 --> 00:21:51,179
Just one rule.

377
00:21:51,212 --> 00:21:52,847
WIN!

378
00:21:52,880 --> 00:21:54,615
All right, you mutts.
[mic feedbacks]

379
00:21:54,649 --> 00:21:56,449
Give them what they want.

380
00:21:57,285 --> 00:21:58,820
[intense music]

381
00:21:58,853 --> 00:22:00,888
Let's go!

382
00:22:04,258 --> 00:22:06,426
[intense hype music]

383
00:22:12,133 --> 00:22:13,167
[body thuds]

384
00:22:13,201 --> 00:22:15,368
-Not so tough now, motherfucker!

385
00:22:15,402 --> 00:22:17,538
-[man] Get up, you shit.

386
00:22:20,741 --> 00:22:22,475
[punches thrown]

387
00:22:22,510 --> 00:22:25,079
[audience clamoring]

388
00:22:25,112 --> 00:22:27,215
-[man] Come on.
Get up.

389
00:22:27,248 --> 00:22:29,250
Let's go!

390
00:22:29,283 --> 00:22:30,718
[body thuds]

391
00:22:32,086 --> 00:22:32,987
[throws kick]
[neck snaps]

392
00:22:33,020 --> 00:22:34,387
[blood spurts]

393
00:22:34,421 --> 00:22:38,559
[audience cheers and whoops]

394
00:22:41,361 --> 00:22:42,630
-[shrieks]

395
00:22:43,965 --> 00:22:45,398
[audience cheers and whoops]

396
00:22:47,168 --> 00:22:48,368
-[man] Let's go!

397
00:22:48,401 --> 00:22:50,571
-[Doyle] Come on, get up!

398
00:22:53,107 --> 00:22:54,242
[kick thrown]

399
00:22:54,275 --> 00:22:55,475
[body thuds]

400
00:22:55,509 --> 00:22:57,111
[audience cheers and whoops]

401
00:23:01,782 --> 00:23:03,284
-[laughs]

402
00:23:03,317 --> 00:23:05,319
You are one cocky
son of a bitch,

403
00:23:05,353 --> 00:23:06,486
I'll give you that.

404
00:23:06,520 --> 00:23:07,855
-He almost had me a few times.

405
00:23:07,889 --> 00:23:09,590
-Ah! You're the one
still standing.

406
00:23:09,624 --> 00:23:11,025
That's all that matters.

407
00:23:11,959 --> 00:23:12,894
-[Bender] Well done.

408
00:23:12,927 --> 00:23:15,062
All right, Tommy,
let's get you cleaned up.

409
00:23:16,330 --> 00:23:17,999
-[Doyle] Atlas.

410
00:23:21,636 --> 00:23:23,470
What did you think
of The Bomber?

411
00:23:23,504 --> 00:23:25,239
-What do you want me to say?

412
00:23:25,273 --> 00:23:26,674
He's good?

413
00:23:26,707 --> 00:23:28,042
-Well, Clay's going to need
for you to set up

414
00:23:28,075 --> 00:23:29,110
a couple more fights for him.

415
00:23:29,143 --> 00:23:31,012
-All right.
That's what we do.

416
00:23:31,045 --> 00:23:32,213
I'll set him up.

417
00:23:32,246 --> 00:23:33,681
-Well, he wants
to see him fight Tommy.

418
00:23:33,714 --> 00:23:37,018
-Nah. Let's do a few
more fights first.

419
00:23:37,051 --> 00:23:38,386
Build him up a little.

420
00:23:38,418 --> 00:23:41,656
-No. You set it up now
with your rabid dog.

421
00:23:42,790 --> 00:23:44,292
-First of all,

422
00:23:44,325 --> 00:23:46,493
you ever talk to me
like that ever again,

423
00:23:46,527 --> 00:23:48,329
I'll fucking kill you.

424
00:23:48,362 --> 00:23:50,398
Now message boy,

425
00:23:50,430 --> 00:23:53,200
you tell Clay
he's got a problem with me.

426
00:23:53,234 --> 00:23:54,735
Don't take it out on Tommy.

427
00:23:54,769 --> 00:23:57,204
-You think you call the shots?

428
00:23:57,238 --> 00:23:59,640
You're on a tight leash...boy.

429
00:23:59,674 --> 00:24:02,576
[scoffs] Don't you forget it.

430
00:24:08,983 --> 00:24:11,953
[engine revving]

431
00:24:15,389 --> 00:24:17,258
-[Bender] Hey, Ray.
-Bender.

432
00:24:17,291 --> 00:24:19,627
-You have fun tonight?

433
00:24:19,660 --> 00:24:21,062
-Your boy's a stud.

434
00:24:21,095 --> 00:24:22,096
Definitely talented.

435
00:24:22,129 --> 00:24:23,631
-Yeah. You put any money on him?

436
00:24:23,664 --> 00:24:25,633
-You trying to get me
in trouble?

437
00:24:25,666 --> 00:24:28,069
-[chuckles] What an upstanding
citizen like you.

438
00:24:28,102 --> 00:24:28,903
What are we talking about?

439
00:24:28,936 --> 00:24:31,105
I'm not going to get you
in trouble.

440
00:24:31,138 --> 00:24:33,007
-How's everything?

441
00:24:34,575 --> 00:24:36,544
-Same old, same old, brother.

442
00:24:38,012 --> 00:24:40,681
For the, uh,
department of morale fund.

443
00:24:40,715 --> 00:24:42,550
-All right.
You got it.

444
00:24:42,583 --> 00:24:45,219
[engine starting]

445
00:24:48,456 --> 00:24:50,591
-Your guy from the force?

446
00:24:50,624 --> 00:24:53,260
-Yeah, it was Dutch's idea
to put him on payroll.

447
00:24:53,294 --> 00:24:55,429
Kept the heat off us
all these years.

448
00:24:55,463 --> 00:24:57,064
-You trust him?

449
00:24:58,165 --> 00:25:00,368
-He hasn't let me down yet.

450
00:25:00,401 --> 00:25:03,971
-Good. Keep me in the loop.

451
00:25:04,005 --> 00:25:06,941
I want you to go with Tommy
and see my friend in Chinatown.

452
00:25:06,974 --> 00:25:07,875
All right?

453
00:25:07,908 --> 00:25:10,144
Take some of the boys as well.

454
00:25:10,177 --> 00:25:12,013
Let them blow off some steam.

455
00:25:12,046 --> 00:25:14,115
It's been a good night.

456
00:25:14,148 --> 00:25:15,082
-You aren't not coming?

457
00:25:15,116 --> 00:25:16,951
-Not tonight.

458
00:25:21,055 --> 00:25:24,091
[upbeat music]

459
00:25:31,732 --> 00:25:33,200
-Hi. How many guests?

460
00:25:33,234 --> 00:25:35,002
-I think we've got 12 all in.

461
00:25:35,036 --> 00:25:37,905
You should have
a table last name, King.

462
00:25:37,938 --> 00:25:38,806
-Yes, we do.

463
00:25:38,839 --> 00:25:40,141
We got that all ready
for you guys.

464
00:25:40,174 --> 00:25:41,475
-Awesome.
Can you take them to the table?

465
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:42,576
-Yeah.

466
00:25:42,610 --> 00:25:44,645
-Man, yo,
keep the ladies lit, man.

467
00:25:44,678 --> 00:25:46,180
Keep the party going, man.

468
00:25:46,213 --> 00:25:47,448
Shit, man.
Oh, man.

469
00:25:47,481 --> 00:25:48,783
I can't even [indistinct]

470
00:25:48,816 --> 00:25:50,384
I hope you're talking
about getting my money back.

471
00:25:50,418 --> 00:25:51,318
'Cause you lost the fight
over here.

472
00:25:51,352 --> 00:25:52,353
What are you doing?

473
00:25:52,386 --> 00:25:54,622
Let's go, man.
Get out of here.

474
00:25:54,655 --> 00:25:57,091
I'm not all that easy.

475
00:25:57,124 --> 00:25:58,893
-[Tommy] Yeah, whatever.

476
00:26:00,694 --> 00:26:03,264
I know you from somewhere?

477
00:26:03,297 --> 00:26:05,466
-I don't think so.

478
00:26:05,499 --> 00:26:07,168
-Are you sure?

479
00:26:07,201 --> 00:26:09,070
-I'd remember.

480
00:26:12,507 --> 00:26:14,575
-Uh, is Mr. Kwan around?

481
00:26:14,608 --> 00:26:16,610
Can you take me to him?

482
00:26:17,478 --> 00:26:19,246
-Follow me.

483
00:26:20,247 --> 00:26:23,684
[upbeat, ethereal music]

484
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:28,122
-[muffled laughter]

485
00:26:34,328 --> 00:26:37,665
[upbeat, ethereal music
continues]

486
00:26:41,635 --> 00:26:44,004
-[Colette] Mr. Kwan,
someone's here to see you.

487
00:26:45,172 --> 00:26:48,175
[muffled upbeat music]

488
00:26:50,344 --> 00:26:52,680
-[Tommy] Atlas King sent me.

489
00:26:55,182 --> 00:26:57,418
-You Dutch's boy?

490
00:26:57,451 --> 00:26:58,786
-Yeah, that's right.

491
00:26:58,819 --> 00:27:00,888
-We did business together.

492
00:27:00,921 --> 00:27:03,257
-[Tommy] Atlas told me that.

493
00:27:04,425 --> 00:27:06,360
Ten grand?

494
00:27:09,130 --> 00:27:10,865
[envelope rustles]

495
00:27:12,766 --> 00:27:14,135
-[straining] Ah.

496
00:27:14,168 --> 00:27:17,171
These are blueprints
for a stash house in Chinatown.

497
00:27:17,204 --> 00:27:19,306
All the details are there.

498
00:27:19,340 --> 00:27:21,775
Kickbacks, bookies, [sighs]

499
00:27:21,809 --> 00:27:23,512
protection money
all go through there.

500
00:27:23,545 --> 00:27:26,615
Triads rotate the location
every month.

501
00:27:26,647 --> 00:27:29,551
[laughs]
But there's only so many,

502
00:27:29,584 --> 00:27:31,452
uh, secure spots they can use.

503
00:27:31,485 --> 00:27:34,388
Eventually, pattern repeats.

504
00:27:34,421 --> 00:27:38,058
At the end of this month,
they'll circle back to that one.

505
00:27:38,092 --> 00:27:40,294
-And where'd you get
all this information?

506
00:27:40,327 --> 00:27:43,364
-[chuckles] You tell Atlas
that I'll get him

507
00:27:43,397 --> 00:27:47,501
with a drop schedule, amount,
and entry points next week.

508
00:27:47,536 --> 00:27:51,005
And I get 10% of the take.

509
00:27:55,176 --> 00:27:58,412
[upbeat hype music]

510
00:28:02,883 --> 00:28:05,719
[clubbers whooping]

511
00:28:09,591 --> 00:28:12,693
[upbeat hype music]

512
00:28:17,097 --> 00:28:18,365
[door opens]

513
00:28:19,668 --> 00:28:22,604
-What are you doing in my chair?

514
00:28:22,637 --> 00:28:26,106
-I think you need
better security.

515
00:28:26,140 --> 00:28:28,075
Twenty-five grand.

516
00:28:28,108 --> 00:28:30,911
Half of what's owed to Emerson.

517
00:28:30,945 --> 00:28:33,714
I'll have the rest
at the end of the month.

518
00:28:33,747 --> 00:28:36,016
-Do I need to count it?

519
00:28:36,050 --> 00:28:38,252
-Only if you want to spend
more time with me.

520
00:28:38,285 --> 00:28:41,422
[distant siren blaring]

521
00:28:41,455 --> 00:28:44,225
-You could have called,
you know.

522
00:28:45,092 --> 00:28:48,095
-I didn't know
you wanted to see me.

523
00:28:50,097 --> 00:28:52,866
-You could have called
at least once.

524
00:28:52,900 --> 00:28:56,203
Just a hello or something.

525
00:28:56,237 --> 00:29:00,241
"I'm alive.
Don't worry about me.

526
00:29:00,274 --> 00:29:03,010
I'm sorry I left."

527
00:29:04,646 --> 00:29:06,514
Anything, you know.

528
00:29:06,548 --> 00:29:08,115
I think I deserved it.

529
00:29:08,148 --> 00:29:09,316
-[sighs]

530
00:29:09,350 --> 00:29:12,587
[inhales, exhales]

531
00:29:12,621 --> 00:29:14,888
Wouldn't have changed anything.

532
00:29:23,397 --> 00:29:24,999
[lip smacks]

533
00:29:30,471 --> 00:29:36,377
-Whatever we had,
it expired a long time ago.

534
00:29:37,845 --> 00:29:40,047
-I don't blame you.

535
00:29:40,914 --> 00:29:43,083
Just had to know for sure.

536
00:29:45,654 --> 00:29:48,055
-[light chuckle]
What are you doing here?

537
00:29:48,088 --> 00:29:49,957
-I know Clay shored up money
for the casino

538
00:29:49,990 --> 00:29:51,693
he's trying to build.

539
00:29:51,726 --> 00:29:53,494
-You seem to know a lot.

540
00:29:53,528 --> 00:29:56,330
-[soft chuckle]
He needs capital.

541
00:29:56,363 --> 00:29:59,567
More than the money
he's squeezing from us.

542
00:29:59,601 --> 00:30:01,603
So I got a proposition for him.

543
00:30:01,636 --> 00:30:04,305
It will help him
with his casino.

544
00:30:04,338 --> 00:30:06,807
Clear my debt for good.

545
00:30:10,645 --> 00:30:12,714
-Last time you tangled
with Clay,

546
00:30:12,747 --> 00:30:15,249
he almost killed you.

547
00:30:15,282 --> 00:30:18,886
This time,
he'll finish the job.

548
00:30:18,919 --> 00:30:22,724
-Just set the meeting.
Leave the rest to me.

549
00:30:22,757 --> 00:30:24,858
All right?

550
00:30:26,960 --> 00:30:31,899
You know, eventually,
he'll turn on you as well.

551
00:30:32,966 --> 00:30:37,338
-I know.
I have an exit plan.

552
00:30:37,371 --> 00:30:39,840
Make sure you do too.

553
00:30:41,208 --> 00:30:42,843
[sighs]

554
00:30:42,876 --> 00:30:46,213
[distant clubbers cheering
and whooping]

555
00:30:46,246 --> 00:30:50,184
[upbeat music]

556
00:30:50,217 --> 00:30:52,019
<i>♪ Come and dance with me ♪</i>

557
00:30:52,052 --> 00:30:54,922
<i>♪ Come and dance with me ♪</i>

558
00:30:54,955 --> 00:30:56,758
<i>♪ Come and dance with me ♪</i>

559
00:30:56,791 --> 00:30:58,092
<i>♪ Come and dance with me ♪</i>

560
00:30:58,125 --> 00:30:59,326
-[singing "Butterfly"
by Crazy Town plays]

561
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,028
<i>♪ Come my lady</i>
<i>come-come my lady ♪</i>

562
00:31:01,061 --> 00:31:03,964
<i>♪ You're my butterfly,</i>
<i>sugar baby ♪</i>

563
00:31:08,001 --> 00:31:09,069
<i>♪ Come my lady ♪</i>

564
00:31:09,103 --> 00:31:10,371
<i>♪ Come-come my lady ♪</i>

565
00:31:10,404 --> 00:31:13,006
<i>♪ You're my butterfly,</i>
<i>sugar baby ♪</i>

566
00:31:13,040 --> 00:31:14,576
<i>♪ Come my lady... ♪</i>

567
00:31:14,609 --> 00:31:16,477
-You talk to Kwan?

568
00:31:16,511 --> 00:31:17,746
-Yeah, it's all set.

569
00:31:17,779 --> 00:31:19,547
-Great.

570
00:31:23,250 --> 00:31:26,755
-But for real, yo,
that was a good fight.

571
00:31:26,788 --> 00:31:29,758
But the fights back in the day
was crazy.

572
00:31:29,791 --> 00:31:31,559
I'm talking no rules.

573
00:31:31,593 --> 00:31:33,026
No ropes.

574
00:31:33,060 --> 00:31:36,765
Sucker kicks to the face,
smashed teeth.

575
00:31:36,798 --> 00:31:39,900
Now you guys are fighting
for the crowd.

576
00:31:39,933 --> 00:31:43,137
Back then,
they was fighting for survival.

577
00:31:43,170 --> 00:31:46,674
And Atlas King,
he ruled the ring.

578
00:31:46,708 --> 00:31:49,910
[muffled dramatic music]

579
00:31:51,011 --> 00:31:52,112
-Dude, you saw him fight?

580
00:31:52,146 --> 00:31:54,114
[muffled blow lands]

581
00:31:54,148 --> 00:31:57,384
-I saw him knock a guy out
in ten seconds,

582
00:31:57,418 --> 00:31:58,620
break his jaw,

583
00:31:58,653 --> 00:32:03,957
and still give him his cut
like it was all business.

584
00:32:03,991 --> 00:32:08,162
Heh, cold-blooded. Shit.

585
00:32:10,063 --> 00:32:13,200
I remember when Clay Emerson,

586
00:32:14,501 --> 00:32:17,204
he tried to make Atlas King
take a fall.

587
00:32:17,237 --> 00:32:21,008
He didn't even bend.
And then you know what he did?

588
00:32:21,041 --> 00:32:23,444
He demolished his golden boy

589
00:32:23,477 --> 00:32:26,113
in front of everyone.
[muffled blow lands]

590
00:32:26,146 --> 00:32:30,919
And that's when Clay tried
to take a shot at Atlas King.

591
00:32:30,951 --> 00:32:33,487
He wanted to make
an example out of him.

592
00:32:33,521 --> 00:32:37,124
So Dutch got him out
with a bullet in him.

593
00:32:37,157 --> 00:32:39,960
-How come Dutch and Atlas
didn't just take Clay head-on?

594
00:32:39,993 --> 00:32:41,495
-Clay would erase you.

595
00:32:41,529 --> 00:32:44,331
No name, no nothing.

596
00:32:44,364 --> 00:32:48,001
He would burn
this whole shit down.

597
00:32:48,837 --> 00:32:50,705
No, see. No shit.

598
00:32:50,738 --> 00:32:53,808
-How long you been
sitting on that?

599
00:32:53,842 --> 00:32:55,476
[Eddie sighs]

600
00:32:58,078 --> 00:32:59,112
[upbeat hype music]

601
00:32:59,146 --> 00:33:01,516
-God, Whitney, don't.

602
00:33:01,549 --> 00:33:03,016
Ah! You're killing me!

603
00:33:03,050 --> 00:33:04,652
-[Bender groans]

604
00:33:04,686 --> 00:33:09,089
[laughs] I'll get 'em home.

605
00:33:10,625 --> 00:33:12,459
Do you need a ride?

606
00:33:12,493 --> 00:33:15,429
-No, I'm, uh,
gonna catch you later.

607
00:33:15,462 --> 00:33:17,130
-Um...

608
00:33:17,164 --> 00:33:18,098
Yeah, there's something
I've been wanting

609
00:33:18,131 --> 00:33:19,233
to talk to you about,

610
00:33:19,266 --> 00:33:21,636
and I didn't know
if the time was right

611
00:33:21,669 --> 00:33:24,204
with your dad passing.

612
00:33:24,238 --> 00:33:27,509
But me and Penelope,

613
00:33:28,810 --> 00:33:31,078
I was gonna propose.

614
00:33:32,881 --> 00:33:37,317
Look, I know--I know your dad
never wanted this life for her,

615
00:33:37,351 --> 00:33:41,488
but, um, you know,
I'm gonna get a fresh start,

616
00:33:41,523 --> 00:33:43,591
clean slate.

617
00:33:43,625 --> 00:33:45,894
I just...

618
00:33:45,927 --> 00:33:50,197
I was gonna ask him
for her hand.

619
00:33:51,933 --> 00:33:54,769
-Well, as long as
that's what she wants,

620
00:33:54,802 --> 00:33:56,336
it's her decision.

621
00:33:56,370 --> 00:33:58,573
And Dutch
would have said the same.

622
00:33:58,606 --> 00:34:01,776
Hey, man,
she really cares about you.

623
00:34:03,443 --> 00:34:05,647
[shake hands]
-Thanks, bro.

624
00:34:07,214 --> 00:34:09,951
-Man, cut this lovey-dovey
shit out, man.

625
00:34:09,984 --> 00:34:11,151
We outta here.

626
00:34:11,184 --> 00:34:12,987
-Aight. We'll catch up tomorrow.
-Let's go, man.

627
00:34:13,021 --> 00:34:14,689
-[Bender] All right,
all right, all right.

628
00:34:24,231 --> 00:34:26,801
[upbeat club music]

629
00:34:32,740 --> 00:34:34,809
-Your friends are crazy.

630
00:34:36,176 --> 00:34:38,813
-Yeah, they're
a terrible influence.

631
00:34:40,982 --> 00:34:43,216
-Got a light?

632
00:34:45,352 --> 00:34:48,155
[upbeat club music continues]

633
00:34:48,188 --> 00:34:49,657
[ashtray clinks]

634
00:34:58,432 --> 00:34:59,701
-Tommy.

635
00:35:01,134 --> 00:35:02,904
Never got your name.

636
00:35:02,937 --> 00:35:04,872
-I never gave it.

637
00:35:08,643 --> 00:35:10,477
I've seen you fight.

638
00:35:11,478 --> 00:35:13,146
Such a temper.

639
00:35:13,948 --> 00:35:15,950
-Yeah, it's therapeutic.

640
00:35:15,984 --> 00:35:18,318
-Is that what you tell yourself?

641
00:35:18,352 --> 00:35:20,454
-It's my only playground.

642
00:35:20,487 --> 00:35:22,523
I mean, I'm lucky to have one.

643
00:35:22,557 --> 00:35:25,292
Most people don't even
have their own.

644
00:35:25,325 --> 00:35:27,762
-Where did you hear that?

645
00:35:29,063 --> 00:35:30,263
-I read it in a book.

646
00:35:30,297 --> 00:35:32,934
-Oh, wow!
You read?

647
00:35:32,967 --> 00:35:35,603
-I have my moments.
-Mm.

648
00:35:37,739 --> 00:35:39,774
You on a break?

649
00:35:39,807 --> 00:35:41,843
-My shift just ended.

650
00:35:43,176 --> 00:35:45,178
-You wanna get outta here?

651
00:35:45,212 --> 00:35:46,681
[car honking]

652
00:35:46,714 --> 00:35:49,149
[distant siren wailing]

653
00:35:52,352 --> 00:35:53,688
[distant alarm beeping]

654
00:35:53,721 --> 00:35:57,692
[Tommy groans sleepily]

655
00:35:57,725 --> 00:36:00,595
[distant siren wailing]

656
00:36:59,153 --> 00:37:02,590
[cards rustling]

657
00:37:03,991 --> 00:37:06,060
-[sleepy groan]

658
00:37:06,094 --> 00:37:08,228
-[Tommy]
I didn't mean to wake you.

659
00:37:15,636 --> 00:37:17,404
[lighter flicks]

660
00:37:19,841 --> 00:37:21,008
-[sighs]

661
00:37:22,375 --> 00:37:24,579
You always jump in bed
with strangers?

662
00:37:25,913 --> 00:37:27,982
-Whenever I can.

663
00:37:30,651 --> 00:37:32,252
-[blows smoke]

664
00:37:33,054 --> 00:37:34,889
-Are you a dancer?

665
00:37:37,792 --> 00:37:39,160
-You wanna come?

666
00:37:39,193 --> 00:37:40,962
See me dance?

667
00:37:42,163 --> 00:37:44,799
I'm there every night
before work.

668
00:37:47,467 --> 00:37:49,504
Come by one of these days.

669
00:37:54,208 --> 00:37:56,476
-You gonna tell me your name?

670
00:37:59,446 --> 00:38:01,549
-If I see you again.

671
00:38:06,087 --> 00:38:07,855
-I gotta run.

672
00:38:09,322 --> 00:38:11,793
-[clicks tongue]
I didn't ask you to stay.

673
00:38:11,826 --> 00:38:12,794
[cigarette crackling]

674
00:38:21,235 --> 00:38:22,970
[door closes]

675
00:38:25,973 --> 00:38:27,575
[sighs]

676
00:38:32,814 --> 00:38:34,882
[birds chirping]

677
00:38:43,390 --> 00:38:45,760
-[blows smoke]

678
00:38:49,096 --> 00:38:50,998
[plates clattering gently]

679
00:38:52,967 --> 00:38:54,367
[gate creaks open]

680
00:38:54,401 --> 00:38:56,137
-[Penelope] Hey.

681
00:38:56,170 --> 00:38:57,337
[gate rattling]

682
00:38:57,370 --> 00:38:59,207
I ask you to come at 11,
you come at 12?

683
00:38:59,240 --> 00:39:00,675
-Is that how you talk
to a champ?

684
00:39:00,708 --> 00:39:02,076
-Oh, champ, huh? [chuckles]

685
00:39:02,109 --> 00:39:03,978
A champ who can't figure out
how to get me two baguettes?

686
00:39:04,011 --> 00:39:06,247
That's a ciabatta,
what's the matter with you?

687
00:39:06,280 --> 00:39:08,049
How was the fight?

688
00:39:08,082 --> 00:39:09,851
-[Tommy] I knocked him out.

689
00:39:09,884 --> 00:39:11,853
-Attaboy.

690
00:39:13,353 --> 00:39:16,557
[birds chirping]

691
00:39:19,894 --> 00:39:22,730
I'm worried about you.

692
00:39:22,763 --> 00:39:26,300
-Well, that's part
of the job description.

693
00:39:26,334 --> 00:39:29,237
-Thought you'd be out
of this by now.

694
00:39:29,270 --> 00:39:30,338
Saw what happened to Dad,

695
00:39:30,370 --> 00:39:32,740
I don't want that happening
to you too.

696
00:39:34,308 --> 00:39:36,310
[birds chirping]

697
00:39:36,344 --> 00:39:39,146
-Atlas is gonna meet
with Emerson.

698
00:39:39,180 --> 00:39:41,582
We're gonna find a way
to cut loose once and for all.

699
00:39:41,616 --> 00:39:44,484
I mean, like,
it's coming soon.

700
00:39:44,518 --> 00:39:48,022
-Which is exactly
what Dad used to say.

701
00:39:48,055 --> 00:39:50,157
And he never got out, did he?

702
00:39:55,596 --> 00:39:59,499
The thing he hated most of all
was that he got you involved.

703
00:40:01,501 --> 00:40:05,039
Mom never forgave him for that.

704
00:40:05,072 --> 00:40:08,309
-He never forced me to do
anything I didn't want to.

705
00:40:08,342 --> 00:40:11,646
This was just a hand
that was dealt to us.

706
00:40:11,679 --> 00:40:13,848
-Okay, fine, but he's gone now,

707
00:40:13,881 --> 00:40:17,618
which means it's up to you
to get yourself out.

708
00:40:17,652 --> 00:40:19,186
Before it's too late.

709
00:40:19,220 --> 00:40:21,923
[footsteps approaching]

710
00:40:21,956 --> 00:40:23,190
-[Bender] What'd I miss?

711
00:40:23,224 --> 00:40:25,059
[chair scrapes]

712
00:40:25,092 --> 00:40:27,161
-Uh, lunch.

713
00:40:27,194 --> 00:40:28,963
-Morning, Sleeping Beauty.

714
00:40:28,996 --> 00:40:33,100
-[sighs] What'd you wind up
getting into last night?

715
00:40:33,134 --> 00:40:37,605
-Uh, I ran into that hostess
after you guys took off.

716
00:40:39,273 --> 00:40:40,374
-Nice.

717
00:40:40,408 --> 00:40:42,109
-Oh yeah?
We got somebody new?

718
00:40:42,143 --> 00:40:43,878
-[Tommy] Don't start.

719
00:40:43,911 --> 00:40:45,445
-Sorry,
I'm just asking questions.

720
00:40:45,478 --> 00:40:49,016
Please get your feet off
of my furniture, you animal.

721
00:40:50,151 --> 00:40:52,520
-What you getting into now?

722
00:40:52,553 --> 00:40:53,788
-[Tommy] I'm gonna head
to the gym.

723
00:40:53,821 --> 00:40:54,989
-[sighs]

724
00:40:55,923 --> 00:40:59,894
-Alright. I'll catch up
with you after.

725
00:41:01,062 --> 00:41:02,462
Oh, thank you.

726
00:41:02,495 --> 00:41:04,899
-[Penelope giggles]
-[Bender] Thank you.

727
00:41:07,134 --> 00:41:10,972
[intriguing music]

728
00:41:11,005 --> 00:41:14,041
[train rattling]

729
00:41:15,376 --> 00:41:16,911
[train door hisses]

730
00:41:18,012 --> 00:41:20,480
[train rattling]

731
00:41:20,514 --> 00:41:23,651
[pensive music]

732
00:41:43,471 --> 00:41:45,673
-Take her upstairs [indistinct]

733
00:41:48,109 --> 00:41:52,780
[intriguing music]

734
00:41:56,384 --> 00:41:57,852
[door squeaks]

735
00:41:58,886 --> 00:42:00,988
-Hey, what's up?
-[trainer] Go!

736
00:42:01,022 --> 00:42:02,289
One, two.

737
00:42:02,323 --> 00:42:04,258
[upbeat music]

738
00:42:04,291 --> 00:42:05,926
[grunts]

739
00:42:08,629 --> 00:42:09,930
Yeah. Lift your knee

740
00:42:09,964 --> 00:42:12,700
and measure the distance
and strength.

741
00:42:13,434 --> 00:42:14,635
-The knee goes right up.

742
00:42:14,668 --> 00:42:16,037
-[Tommy] Alright.

743
00:42:17,004 --> 00:42:17,838
[panting]

744
00:42:17,872 --> 00:42:20,608
-[Tommy grunting]
-Nice.

745
00:42:23,210 --> 00:42:24,545
Bounce around.
One, two.

746
00:42:24,578 --> 00:42:26,080
[kick lands]

747
00:42:26,113 --> 00:42:27,581
Nice. Be more explosive.

748
00:42:27,615 --> 00:42:30,718
[punching bag thumps]

749
00:42:30,751 --> 00:42:33,587
[panting, grunting]

750
00:42:33,621 --> 00:42:35,524
One, two.

751
00:42:35,589 --> 00:42:38,726
Tommy.
You ready to hit the pads?

752
00:42:38,759 --> 00:42:42,129
Bomber's in the cage, training.

753
00:42:42,163 --> 00:42:43,998
He's fucking good.

754
00:42:44,031 --> 00:42:46,400
Maybe you should get in there
with him and see if he'll roll.

755
00:42:46,434 --> 00:42:48,537
Look, Clay is pushing
for this fight.

756
00:42:48,569 --> 00:42:51,472
Why not? Get in there
and see what he's about.

757
00:42:51,506 --> 00:42:53,674
-No sweat.

758
00:42:53,707 --> 00:42:54,942
[The Bomber grunts]
[kick thrown]

759
00:42:59,480 --> 00:43:01,348
[The Bomber strains]

760
00:43:01,382 --> 00:43:03,084
-They tell me
we're fighting soon.

761
00:43:03,117 --> 00:43:04,785
[kick lands]

762
00:43:06,687 --> 00:43:09,323
[indistinct chatter
in the background]

763
00:43:09,356 --> 00:43:11,258
-I'll put you
to sleep real quick.

764
00:43:11,292 --> 00:43:12,893
-I've heard it before.

765
00:43:12,927 --> 00:43:16,030
Virgil, keep your boy in check.

766
00:43:16,063 --> 00:43:19,967
-What happens outside the venue
is not my problem.

767
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:22,036
-You wanna go?

768
00:43:22,069 --> 00:43:23,370
-Bring it.

769
00:43:23,404 --> 00:43:24,638
-Ooh, man!

770
00:43:24,672 --> 00:43:27,608
[indistinct chatter]

771
00:43:27,641 --> 00:43:29,477
-[Virgil] Just a friendly roll,
fellas.

772
00:43:29,511 --> 00:43:31,145
No punching.

773
00:43:33,347 --> 00:43:34,516
[door closes]

774
00:43:34,549 --> 00:43:37,751
[indistinct chatter]

775
00:43:37,785 --> 00:43:39,653
-[Virgil] Let's go.

776
00:43:39,687 --> 00:43:41,322
You got this.

777
00:43:42,423 --> 00:43:44,758
[tense music]

778
00:43:44,792 --> 00:43:46,494
[indistinct chatter]

779
00:43:46,528 --> 00:43:48,095
You got this. Come on!

780
00:43:49,396 --> 00:43:50,631
[onlookers clamoring]

781
00:43:50,664 --> 00:43:52,766
-[grunting]

782
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:54,468
-[man] Let's go, Bomber!

783
00:43:54,502 --> 00:43:55,769
-[man 2]
Hey, what are you doing?

784
00:43:55,803 --> 00:43:57,539
[overlapping grunting]

785
00:43:57,572 --> 00:43:59,140
[onlookers clamoring]

786
00:43:59,173 --> 00:44:01,142
-[Virgil] That's it.
That's it, champ.

787
00:44:01,175 --> 00:44:03,110
You got it.

788
00:44:04,211 --> 00:44:06,313
-[man] Roll him. Roll him!

789
